+ATTEMPT 2: THE CHECK TIMEOUT
+
+Attempt 1 exited rc=0 with gates 0-7 green in ~25 min, but ringer's check killed at its 60 s ceiling.
+Root cause, measured live in this session: this host's WSL resolver (10.255.255.254) stalls ~10 s on every AAAA query while A-only lookups answer in milliseconds.
+
+  $ time getent ahostsv4 api.github.com   -> real 0m0.005s
+  $ time getent ahostsv6 api.github.com   -> real 0m11.611s
+  $ time getent hosts codeload.github.com -> real 0m10.031s  (A+AAAA combined)
+
+gh is a statically built Go binary, so GODEBUG=netdns=cgo and RES_OPTIONS cannot steer it (both measured: no effect, still 10-11 s), and Go's resolver always issues A+AAAA in parallel, so every gh process paid the stall.
+The suite makes 163 gh process calls (profiled), which is the whole ~25 min: 163 x ~10 s.
+Pinning api.github.com in a namespace-private /etc/hosts drops a gh call from 11.7 s to 0.199 s (both measured).
+
+WHAT I FIXED (repair 2)
+
+tests/receipt-gates.sh only: a preamble before Gate 0 that resolves api.github.com and github.com A-only, writes them into a mount-namespace-private /etc/hosts, and re-execs the suite inside `unshare -rm` with that bind mount.
+No system file is touched, addresses are re-resolved on every run, and a host without unprivileged namespaces falls through unpinned with a loud note (same assertions, only slower).
+The helper is untouched this attempt; no gate byte is touched (diff against the u04.patch original shows exactly: preamble + Gate 7 + final PASS line, nothing else).
+
+Measured result: `bash tests/receipt-gates.sh` went from ~25 min to 1m15.3s, exit 0, full output:
